{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics","id":1416613,"title":"Alchemical Cities in Creation, Level 5 Demenses, and geopolitics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-03T05:14:32-07:00","id":1416613,"title":"Alchemical Cities in Creation, Level 5 Demenses, and geopolitics","content":"So I'm trying to create a shard where the majority of the Exalted are Dragonblooded and Alchemicals. Autochthon is down for the count, either dead, in hibernation, or missing. Thankfully the blood of the Dragons are as fecund as ever, and Alchemicals can be built even outside Autochthon. <br /> <br /> The issue is that I now have to build a world where there are at least several hundred Alchemical Exalted. Several hundred Celestial Exalted, all of whom are at worst apathetic and at best actively helping humanity. Hobbled somewhat, yes, and somewhat having limitations that other Exalted don't have. But still exceptionally powerful. <br /> <br /> Ignoring the wider setting questions... <br /> <br /> Let's say that you have a level 5 manse and you plop down an alchemical city down into Creation, somewhere in a place similar to the Threshold. Loads of nasties, Raksha, cholera, and all that stuff. You're counted as lucky if you have a horse or ox to bring your cart to the market, and you are near an urban area if you have a cobblestone road. The old technological primitiveness. And then this Alchemical city smashes its way onto the nearby level 5 manse, with a population of Autochthonians, and a dozen or so Alchemicals. After they finished the shakedown and secure for themselves a source of food and water and essence, they start affecting the world around them. <br /> <br /> The city has municipial charms that help it adapt to the surroundings. A shield against inclement weather. A method of dealing with sewage and fast-growing food and water. And a working knowledge of how Creation works. The question is how would it affect their surroundings? The city has multiple factories, high level crafting and bureaucracy charms, as well as access to champions who are stronger than Dragonblooded if slightly more limited. <br /> <br /> So far I have them as a the equivalent of city-states, with chemical plants inside to create reagants and alchemical products that serve as fertilisers and explosives for mining. Bureaucratic plans are drawn up within the city-states, mean to maximize productivity from the mines and farmlands and trade routes, while the specialized forges within create Superior and Perfect equipment that are the envy of any other craftsmen in the lands. The entire thing is like a bronze age command economy, with a centralized city state taking in the resources from the country side and pumping out more complex products. The only difference is that since its a Celestial Exalt with charms made from the magical materials, the scale is way bigger and the effects are a hell of a lot more effective. <br /> <br /> The political structure is that of City-states. City-states descended from one-another are generally friendly but its not unheard of for them to have a fight. Nation-states defined by borders are rarer now, since there is far far more concentration of power inside individual cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T09:01:02-07:00","id":1416622,"title":"","content":"The Immaculates will definitely preach against it. The entire purpose of the religion is to promote the hegemony of the Dragon-Blooded, and these new arrivals are extreme threats to that. They work with humans rather than lord over them, they have non-Artifact-based technologies beyond anything else in the world which they actively spread, and perhaps worst of all, they actively encourage education for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T09:52:37-07:00","id":1416625,"title":"","content":"Question - what about &quot;Demiurges&quot;? If memory tricks me not there was - at least in 2nd edition, no idea how it will be treated in 3e - the whole conceit about how the people that participate in the process of crafting an Alchemical Exalted are all individuals blessed with some sort of, in the book's words, &quot;connection to the slumbering genius of the Great Maker, allowing the Demiurge to share Autochthon\u2019s nigh-unlimited cognitive bandwidth when learning how to create Alchemical Exalted. This is how a human mind comprehends and implements one-fifth of the Alchemical Exaltation formula, and how a human body\u2019s labors become a direct channel for the power of the Machine God.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, considering that the proccess is not wholy <b>just </b>artifact-crafting, the death of the Machine God might hamper in part or wholy the (re)creation of Alchemicals in Creation or anywhere else, its slumber or disappearance, arguably less so.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not - some case might be made that whatever Workings went on in Autochton's crafting of the Weaving Protocols could take in this role on Autochton's absence, i guess. Alchemical Demiurge definitely has the cost for cover for Thaumaturgy or Sorcery, both of which touch on &quot;esoteric underpinnings of Creation&quot; themes common to all three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-03-2020, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T11:13:35-07:00","id":1416631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416622#post1416622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculates will definitely preach against it. The entire purpose of the religion is to promote the hegemony of the Dragon-Blooded, and these new arrivals are extreme threats to that. They work with humans rather than lord over them, they have non-Artifact-based technologies beyond anything else in the world which they actively spread, and perhaps worst of all, they actively encourage education for all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - The Alchemicals while not labeled as Lords per se are <b>Champions</b>, so far from &quot;just other people&quot; and could be easily understood as another face of the same coin. Also, hello, Lookshy?<br /> <br /> 2 - Their non-Artifact-based technologies might be more ubiquitous indeed, but to say &quot;beyond anything else in the world&quot; seems like a gross exageration to me.<br /> Their crossbows and most clockwork are far from beyond the means of nations with a focus on that, like the Varang City-States.<br /> <br /> 3 - Hello, the Immaculate Order actively actively encourages education of its flock and is the major factor in wholesale spreading of literacy across the breadth of the Blessed Isle? Have you actually read the books?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my 3 little nitpicks, because i <b><i>really </i></b>felt like it was neccessary to bring that up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Weird unrelated aside. Since the subject of Alchemicals was brought up, i have been really bugged by this idea of the weird setting/locales of the old <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZjJmCp97yc4\" target=\"_blank\">Hot Wheels: Acceleracers</a> cartoon as Autochton's circulatory system and some of the strange spirits/machinery that preserves, populate or infect &amp; harm it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-03-2020, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T14:44:23-07:00","id":1416643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416625#post1416625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question - what about &quot;Demiurges&quot;? If memory tricks me not there was - at least in 2nd edition, no idea how it will be treated in 3e - the whole conceit about how the people that participate in the process of crafting an Alchemical Exalted are all individuals blessed with some sort of, in the book's words, &quot;connection to the slumbering genius of the Great Maker, allowing the Demiurge to share<br /> Autochthon\u2019s nigh-unlimited cognitive bandwidth when learning how to create Alchemical Exalted. This is how a human mind comprehends and implements one-fifth of the Alchemical Exaltation formula, and how a human body\u2019s labors become a direct channel for the power of the Machine God.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, considering that the proccess is not wholy <b>just </b>artifact-crafting, the death of the Machine God might hamper in part or wholy the (re)creation of Alchemicals in Creation or anywhere else, its slumber or disappearance, arguably less so.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not - some case might be made that whatever Workings went on in Autochton's crafting of the Weaving Protocols could take in this role on Autochton's absence, i guess. Alchemical Demiurge definitely has the cost for cover for Thaumaturgy or Sorcery, both of which touch on &quot;esoteric underpinnings of Creation&quot; themes common to all three.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this shard some remnant of Autochthon is still active. Maybe its something he preserved within the universe, within every single patropolis, or maybe its some small part of him engraved in the cosmos. But either way, from time to time, men and women of great genius, faith, dogma, and tools, come together to create a singular work of artistry and vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T15:50:54-07:00","id":1416650,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to flesh out how a setting with more alchemicals inside would look like. Definitely more technology. But by how much? After all Alchemical cities are high essence elders who are capable of crafting arifacts far more easily than Dragonblooded. Even ignoring the Artifact question, Alchemical cities have better resources, far better education (there's several homebrewed mass training charms), and probably far more bureaucracy. Farms in the vicinity of an alchemical city might suddenly transition fast to mechanised harvesters and large numbers of specialists that bring in the expertise to build bridges, construct manses, and deal with diseases, there by making shit go far faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T16:55:17-07:00","id":1416656,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> hope your feeling better. Anyway, <i>Ecoonnooomicccs Nerrrrrds, Assemble!</i><br /> <br /> You've just created a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boomtown\" target=\"_blank\">Boom Town</a>. All of the local communities and the nearest City States now have a new weight on the planets-and-trampoline gravity analogy, in an Economic sense. You have a city capable of producing Desirable Goods and everyone around is gonna start doing mental money math to see if they can blow this whole farming thing for a load and become a middleman or merchant at your doorstep. More on that in a second: lets look at your citystate first. <br /> <br /> Since we're living in Fantasy and command economies work (joke of the week, Sors), you have a set of bottlenecks and time constraints. You need X food for Y people which take Z farms W days (assuming food production tech exists and your not just ordinary farming). Well, now you have a population limit, which is a worker limit, which is a goods produced limit. So any trade opportunities work out on a simple Algebra format: Is it beneficial to trade 10 clockwork crossbows (100 manhours) for 50 bushels of wheat (300 manhours?. It becomes a fun little exercise for your economists to work out trade ratios, and then the needs of the Market and surrounding geopolitics changes that valuation. Its basically Recettear/Stardew Valley meets Sim City. <br /> <br /> But of course, you have to take care of those silly <i>people</i> and their dumb <i>wants and needs</i>. Sure you can make wine, tea, and tobacco in your Glass House of Heat for the plebians to have their Luxury Rations, but those ingrates are gonna want to have this thing from the South called <i>Chocolate</i> and so Chocolate merchants come in and people spend their Resource Tokens on outside goods. And then their gonna want <i>different</i> wine, tea, and tobacco from Other Places because its Different. (<b>IMPORTANT</b> jokes aside, don't fall into the idea that Export Good Import Bad. This is probably the biggest giveaway that someone with an opinion on Economics has never studied Economics) This triggers the next thing: Mass Merchant Migration, aka the Boom Town <br /> <br /> So now your Shining Tech City has its staple foodstuff growing and its buying goods from other people and selling them Finished Products (and even Raw Materials like gold which they can't get themselves), so Jan Ni, the ex farmer, is now doing quite well for himself turning Crossbows into Wheat, buying low and selling high. He gets rich. Now everyone who sees him thinks &quot;<i>I bet I could do that too</i>&quot;. So Gre Gori the carpenter who is sick of making furniture all night after a 10 hour day farming decides to open a shop outside Technopolis fixing wagon wheels and selling caravaner stuff to merchants to make their life easier. He buys food with his money. same goes for Blacksmiths, Leatherworkers, Horse.... people, and tailors and everyone else with a side hustle. But they need food since they stopped subsistence farming so now there's a market for other mechants to go farther away and buy food from distant villages and bring it over to feed these people, and they are gonna carry goods back with them to trade for the food, and maybe you can see how this whole thing grows. <br /> <br /> So you have Technopolis chugging away like a (literal) machine while 50 feet out the main door is a boom town of people selling things to Technopolis, and people selling things to them, and distant villages opening new fields and hiring on laborers to provide more food for all these people trying to get rich. Technopolis, like any good communist state, becomes capitalist ('in secret&quot;), because it turns out making Steampunk Gizmos is basically the equivalent of growing food where Trade is concerned, and you can make 100 Light Crystals a day and that becomes Rice measured in tonnage. This is pretty much the point of City Skylines or Stardew where everything is basically solved and all thats left is to spend your money on getting more money and you get bored. <br /> <br /> That's not what happens in here. That's where the swamp gator in the river of trade comes out: <b>Politics</b>. <br /> <br /> So now what you have isn't a city, it isnt a factory, it isn't a utopia of the working man, what you have is a Threat. A threat to people who live in a place called Status Quo and don't like what you're doing to it. Trade isn't a 0 sum game (each person's gain is another's loss) but it <i>can </i>be detrimental to others in the short or even long term. Merchants who used to go to Dynastopia aren't going there, because Light Crystals and Auto Crossbows are more profitable than Candles and Longbows. Technopolis will sell a pound of gold ore for 1000 bushels of wheat, Dynastopia will sell a pound of gold ore for 5000 bushels of wheat, and you have to be an approved gold buyer, which takes political connections, bribes, a daughter to marry off, etc. So in a single year Dynastopia has lost more than half of its merchants, which isn't looking good for a city with landed aristocrats obsessed with status. So they decide to open a frank discussion on trade, productivity, brainstorm new avenues of resource gatheri no I'm fucking around <b>they go to war.</b> <br /> <br /> Dynastopia doesn't really produce paper, ink, wine, tobacco, and rice. Dynastopia produces <b>Violence.</b> and they are quite happy to sell you a receipt for Violence, in the terms of &quot;keep buying our other stuff and we won't sell you Violence&quot;. And you know what? this system works! its great. Nobody else is making Ink, Paper, or Whatever because nobody else can outproduce violence. This is true of real life, but its extra-double-triple true of Exalted which has <i>hereditary super powers</i> and a distinct lack of <i>indiscriminate artillery fusillades</i>. Nobody can compete with Dragonbloods showing up in Magic Armor with Magic Sticks and killing people until peace is declared. So Dynastopia send Technopolis a little friendly note that says &quot;Literally stop existing or we're going to kill the shit out of you and take your stuff&quot; But what's this? Technopolis has it's own domestic production of Violence. Surprise! its war time. <br /> <br /> Dragonblood are a renewable resource but they really don't like being called that. So Dragonblood have to decide if its worth spending Dragonblood ... blood on stopping the Alchemicals but for basically the first time in their life they have opposition, and that opposition has Shiny Fancy Things called <i>Weapons </i>and Dragonblood have been having a great go of other people not having those (in a way that works against artifact armor, etc). So now its gonna become a Siege and people are gonna have to actually Die and if you thought losing merchants was expensive, let me call your attention to how Nation In Bankruptcy level expensive War is. This is where Even Bigger Politics comes out. Essentially, Dynastopia has to get other Citystates and Great Houses to pay for their war, while Technopolis can maybe convince other places to help on Defense. Eventually this is handled between the Major Movers and Shakers and suddenly a ragtag group of homeless omnisexual idiots with golden weapons show up and decide this is Their Problem Now, and yeah, you're in an Adventure Scenario now. <br /> <br /> To sum it all up: 1)City starts making Things, 2)People come for Things, 3)Other people get mad about this -&gt; 4)War? Remember also that up until the very end, <i>the </i><i>exalted played no role in this scenario</i>. The beat of this drum is made of human desire, and exalted can interfere or assist with a lot of stuff, but they ultimately only change the speed of whats going on. <br /> <br /> And that's Economics for you, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T21:12:10-07:00","id":1416675,"title":"","content":"Is this just a setting taking place after the Age of Sorrows? Or a different world with a different history? Makes a bit of a diffetence.<br /> <br /> I had one that sounds similar, but like a true Shard it had a completely different history so things like the Realm, Immaculate Order, even the First Age were not things in setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T21:52:42-07:00","id":1416680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416675#post1416675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this just a setting taking place after the Age of Sorrows? Or a different world with a different history? Makes a bit of a diffetence.<br /> <br /> I had one that sounds similar, but like a true Shard it had a completely different history so things like the Realm, Immaculate Order, even the First Age were not things in setting</div> </div> </div> </div>Different history. Rametheus came back during the age of sorrows. Then things exploded. <br /> <br /> The realm is long gone. And so is the Immaculate order. <br /> <br /> Alchemicals and dragonblooded are all that's left now, with yu shan long since defunct. The Apocalypse has long since passed. And now that they've finished picking over the ruins, they now build new things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T18:08:43-07:00","id":1416782,"title":"","content":"Ok, then anything I could dig up or remember of my Shard wouldn't help<br /> <br /> Sounds interesting though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T19:05:26-07:00","id":1416785,"title":"","content":"Great post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\">Sorcerous Overlord</a>, the discussion of the interplay between economics, changing working relationships, individual desires &amp; politics should make some pretty engrossing fodder and inspiration for the setting up of adventures and intrigue stories.<br /> <br /> Also, definitely going to name Boomtown a southern city-state trying to become a directional power in the firedust trade, thanks for the idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T19:54:21-07:00","id":1416791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416785#post1416785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\">Sorcerous Overlord</a>, the discussion of the discussion of the interplay between economics, changing working relationships, individual desires &amp; politics should make some pretty engrossing fodder and inspiration for the setting up of adventures and intrigue stories.<br /> <br /> Also, definitely going to name Boomtown a southern city-state trying to become a directional power in the firedust trade, thanks for the idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Though I say that the story he makes can be a little bit different. After all, Dragonblooded are dragonblooded, and it would be a mistake to write them off. Dragonblooded can simply take over the nearby merchant operations, being the superlative bureaucrats they can become. Dragonblooded can run the vital mines and resource locations the city needs for its vital glowing crystals, so after establishing a monopoly, start jacking up the prices. Or maybe they act as distributors. After all, they are dragonblooded, and many many people from far away are willing to pay for the light crystals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T02:30:51-07:00","id":1416825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416791#post1416791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I say that the story he makes can be a little bit different. After all, Dragonblooded are dragonblooded, and it would be a mistake to write them off. Dragonblooded can simply take over the nearby merchant operations, being the superlative bureaucrats they can become. Dragonblooded can run the vital mines and resource locations the city needs for its vital glowing crystals, so after establishing a monopoly, start jacking up the prices. Or maybe they act as distributors. After all, they are dragonblooded, and many many people from far away are willing to pay for the light crystals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, yeah, but then the point was to show how those elements may connect to each other in a clear and easy to understand manner that may inspire others.<br /> How much one will extrapolate, improvise on its own or subvert from then onwards, is up to each individual ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T02:56:33-07:00","id":1416829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416791#post1416791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I say that the story he makes can be a little bit different. After all, Dragonblooded are dragonblooded, and it would be a mistake to write them off. Dragonblooded can simply take over the nearby merchant operations, being the superlative bureaucrats they can become. Dragonblooded can run the vital mines and resource locations the city needs for its vital glowing crystals, so after establishing a monopoly, start jacking up the prices. Or maybe they act as distributors. After all, they are dragonblooded, and many many people from far away are willing to pay for the light crystals.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I wrote that i didnt yet know that Society Had Fallen and the normal system of Realm and Dynasts was gone. But to answer your point: can they? If Alchemicals run Technopolis they aren't gonna just watch Deebs set up and take their stuff economically, there will be a back and forth (we can probably assume a rough power balance between the two). The important point in favor of the Roblox is that they have the Technology while the Bloodborne have the Establishment. So each is poised as an Idealogical threat to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T03:12:00-07:00","id":1416831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1416613-alchemical-cities-in-creation-level-5-demenses-and-geopolitics?p=1416829#post1416829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I wrote that i didnt yet know that Society Had Fallen and the normal system of Realm and Dynasts was gone. But to answer your point: can they? If Alchemicals run Technopolis they aren't gonna just watch Deebs set up and take their stuff economically, there will be a back and forth (we can probably assume a rough power balance between the two). The important point in favor of the Roblox is that they have the Technology while the Bloodborne have the Establishment. So each is poised as an Idealogical threat to the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet there's the problem of numbers and spread of power.<br /> <br /> After all, DBs can make more of themselves, don't take much more than a womb and some food to make another one, and if you're good enough at the breeding you can get a pretty consistent supply of superhumans. And their charms can all be learned without extensive technological infrastructure.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Alchemicals are not only limited by the fact that each can bankrupt nations, but also that each needs a heroic soul. And their charms all need to be designed and built. And each charm is an artifact. And they periodically need to go back to their Vats complex. <br /> <br /> So all in all, I think they can be pretty balanced. Probably a tug of war between the two, as bloodlines thin and then thicken, and as Alchemical cities split apart or get destroyed or get built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}